# Flags the CLI accepts that are NOT overrides -- the complement of
# docs/waivers.md. Together the two must account for EVERY flag the parser
# accepts on any verb, so a new flag of any shape fails the sweep until
# somebody has decided which side it is on.
#
# Format:  <flag>  <why it does not lift a refusal>.  ONE ENTRY PER LINE;
# there are no continuation lines, because a parser that reads `flag =
# everything up to the first space` would read an indented continuation as
# a flag named after its first word.
#
# A REASON IS REQUIRED, and it must be a FINISHED SENTENCE: one ending in a
# conjunction or a preposition, or with no sentence-final mark, is a
# finding. Three entries here were truncated mid-clause on the first pass
# -- `--basis`, `--watch-policy` and `--ttl-days` -- and a half-written
# reason is worse than a missing one, because it reads as a judgement that
# somebody made rather than one that was never finished.
#
# Scoping this file by NAME is what it replaces. Three real overrides have
# no `-ok` suffix: --refresh-evidence (takes a sentence), --single-run
# (takes nothing and leaves no trace in the record at all) and --ttl-days
# (takes a number, and an explicit one suppresses ADR-032's decay).

# --- output and machine-readability -------------------------------------
--json  selects machine output; it changes no gate and files nothing.
--ready-json  selects the tracker's JSON shape; a rendering choice only.
--stdin  takes the tracker feed from stdin rather than from a command, which changes where input comes from and nothing about what is admitted.
--live  filters the listing to live claims; read-only.
--stale  filters the listing to stale claims; read-only.
--diverged  filters the listing to diverged claims; read-only.
--retracted  filters the listing to retracted claims; read-only.
--disputed  filters the listing to disputed claims; read-only.
--unverified  filters the listing to unverified claims; read-only.
--cannot-verify  filters the listing to cannot_verify claims; read-only.
--since  narrows an event window; read-only.
--under  narrows a report to one path prefix; read-only.
--exclude  narrows a sweep by pattern; read-only.
--inverse  flips `impact` to ask which files no claim watches; read-only.
--arm  filters `reproduce` to one capsule outcome; read-only.

# --- the content of a filing, not permission to make it -----------------
--text  the claim sentence itself, which is the thing judged rather than a judgement.
--basis  the reasoning basis, and REQUIRED for an INFERRED claim, which makes it the opposite of a waiver: it is demanded, never granted.
--claim  the claim-at-death sentence on `done`; content, and required.
--claim-basis  that claim's own basis; required, so it excuses nothing.
--evidence-cmd  the command whose output becomes the evidence; the screen that may refuse it is lifted by --evidence-unsafe-ok, never by this.
--accept-cmd  the acceptance oracle's command; the screen that may refuse it is lifted by --accept-unsafe-ok, never by this.
--paths  the watch set itself; the budget it may exceed is lifted by --paths-ok, never by this. NOT COVERED BY ANY WAIVER ROW: a `<path>#<selector>` entry is exempt from the one-path and churn budgets by ADR-055, so that exemption is a bypass carried by PATH SYNTAX rather than by a flag, and no register holds it.
--watch-policy  names a watch set reviewed once and reused (FAZA 3); choosing it means the freehand budget is never reached, which is the opposite of lifting it.
--tier  the cost tier; content.
--class  the evidence class; content.
--deps  issue dependencies; content.
--premise  an issue premise; content.
--successor  the id a retraction points at, REQUIRED by `--cause restated`; demanded rather than granted.
--supersedes  the dead premise this link replaces; ADR-013 REFUSES it while the old premise still passes ready, so a refusal acts on it rather than through it.
--cause  ADR-049's retraction cause {restated,expired,wrong}, REQUIRED on every retraction; demanded rather than granted.
--accept-kind  the oracle's kind {verification,validation}; content.

# --- verb selection and mode, not gate lifting --------------------------
--cancel  selects the cancel form of `done`; it chooses a transition.
--reopen  selects the reopen transition; it chooses a transition.
--release  selects the release form of the tag check, which is the stricter form rather than a relaxation.
--recheck  re-executes a recorded capsule; it can only ADD a refusal, never remove one.
--reproduce  re-executes without filing; read-only.
--diff  folds a second ref and prints the delta; read-only.
--mechanical  ADR-012 display subtype on a diverge; it never changes status.
--append-order  selects append order for a batch read; read-only.
